  "@type": "Course",
  "name": "Agents in the Office of the CFO, Banking and Compliance",
  "courseCode": "S2",
  "description": "Put agents to work in the highest-consequence functions of a firm without giving up the professional's judgement. Build finance skill libraries over a unified financial data model, compute an IFRS 9 expected credit loss and a capital adequacy ratio, flag AML threshold breaches and structuring, apply an Islamic finance overlay, and triage an NDA with the human gate in the right place. Each module ends in a graded task that encodes the professional rule. S1 is the recommended starting point; Q2 goes deeper on the credit-risk modelling for those who want it.",
  "url": "https://contexai.pk/courses/s2-agents-cfo-banking-compliance/",
  "provider": {
    "@type": "EducationalOrganization",
    "name": "ContexAi Academy",
    "sameAs": "https://contexai.org"
  },
  "educationalLevel": "Intermediate",
  "teaches": [
    "On successful completion, you will be able to explain how a unified financial data model lets one agent work across different accounting systems.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to apply a mapping rule that converts records from three accounting systems into one common shape.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to calculate a probability-weighted expected credit loss from scenario estimates.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to calculate a capital adequacy ratio and check it against a stated minimum.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to apply threshold and aggregation rules to flag cash transactions for review.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to explain how a Shariah overlay changes the rules an agent follows without replacing the base skill.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to apply a negotiation playbook to sort an NDA into standard or escalate.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to justify why an agent may route a contract for signature but never sign it."
  ],
